  contract conformance 9 passed — 5 response-state positives, 3 negative
                       controls, 1 construct-coverage check, all against
                       contracts/openapi.yaml
  python coverage      97% over src/api (481 statements, 8 missed; floor 80)
  web coverage         99.23% statements / 96.19% branches / 97.22% functions
                       / 99.17% lines over **src/web/app/worklist** — the scope
                       vitest.config.ts sets, six modules and 131 statements,
                       not the whole web tier (floor 80).
                       Both floors were verified to fail when raised above the
                       measured value — in the run that added them (T050, T052),
                       not in this one.
  import contracts     11 kept, 0 broken across three entries — src/api 3,
                       src/model 4, src/gateway 4 — each with a negative fixture
                       enforced by the check that maps declared contracts to
                       fixtures in tests/checks/test_contract_fixtures.py.
                       E010 owns the src/api three.
  ruff                 `check` and `format --check` both clean over all four
                       tiers (gateway 43 files, api 37, model 290, root 577).
  eslint / tsc         clean over src/web — 0 errors. 2 warnings, neither in a
                       file E010 owns (see below).
  mypy                 clean over src/gateway, 18 files, which is the only entry
                       it covers. It does not type-check this feature's code —
                       verify.yml names its step "Type check (gateway)" for that
                       reason, and records that the scope widens when api and
